PRAYER

In the light of the facts and circumstances stated above and in the larger public interest, the Petitioner most respectfully prays that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:

a) Issue an appropriate writ, order or direction, more particularly a writ in the nature of mandamus, directing the Respondents to {primary_relief};

b) Direct constitution of an expert committee / appoint an amicus curiae to assist this Hon'ble Court and to oversee implementation of any directions issued;

c) Direct the Respondents to file affidavit(s) disclosing the steps taken in relation to {subject_matter} and to file periodic compliance reports;

d) Issue continuing mandamus to ensure compliance with the constitutional / statutory mandate;

e) Pending hearing and final disposal of the present petition, grant such interim direction as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit;

f) Pass any other order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the larger public interest and in the interest of justice.

And for this act of kindness, the Petitioner shall ever pray.
